{{!-- What sits under the sign-up card: the upgrade panel, then the route to sign in.

THE PANEL NAMES A REAL PRICE OR IT DOES NOT APPEAR. The design writes "Paid plans start at $8 a
month", which is the cheapest paid tier — so it is queried, ordered by monthly price, and printed
through `{{price}}`. A publication with no paid tier gets no panel rather than an invitation to
plans it does not sell, and `@site.paid_members_enabled` is deliberately not the guard here for
the same reason it is not the guard on the tier switch: it is false until Stripe is connected,
and the plans exist before the payments do.

"See plans" points at Portal rather than at a Membership page, because the Membership page is a
Page a buyer creates and names — the same reason the tag and author archives carry no crumb back
to their directories. Portal's plan chooser is the one address a theme can be sure of.

See auth/sign-in-notes.hbs for why the design's Privacy · Terms line is not carried. --}}
{{#get "tiers" filter="type:paid" order="monthly_price asc" limit="1" as |cheapest|}}
	{{#if cheapest}}
		<div class="border-accent-border bg-accent-soft mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 rounded-md border px-[22px] py-5">
			<p class="font-ui text-muted flex-[1_1_200px] text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55]">
				{{~t "Want everything else too? Paid plans start at {price} a month." price=(price cheapest.[0].monthly_price currency=cheapest.[0].currency)~}}
			</p>

			<a
				href="#/portal/signup"
				data-portal="signup"
				class="btn btn-primary font-ui rounded-sm border px-[18px] py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap no-underline">{{t "See plans"}}</a>
		</div>
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}

<p class="font-ui text-muted mt-6 text-center text-sm">
	{{~t "Already a member?"}}
	<a
		href="#/portal/signin"
		data-portal="signin"
		class="text-accent underline">{{t "Sign in"}}</a>
</p>
